message: "Please cite the technical report and the archived repository release."
title: "A Level-15 Certificate for the Prime-29 Gate in the Fifteen-Runner Lonely Runner Problem"
type: software
abstract: "The prime-29 finite-checking gate for fifteen total runners is closed by proving J(14,29) is empty. A level-one argument leaves one improper orbit. A factor-15 CRT reduction and two independently written exact solvers exclude the coprime branch, while a 210-variable CNF and a DRAT proof checked by DRAT-trim and rate exclude the noncoprime branch. The result contributes log(29) to the finite-checking prime mass but does not prove the full fifteen-runner conjecture."
